# FastAPI Twitter Clone Standards

## Stack and tooling
- Use `uv` for all Python commands and dependencies.
- Run server with `uv run fastapi dev main.py`.
- Lint/format with `uv run ruff check .` and `uv run ruff format .`.
- Do not suggest `pip` workflows unless explicitly requested.

## Architecture expectations
- Keep route logic in `main.py` unless asked to refactor.
- Use server-side rendering with Jinja2 templates in `templates/`.
- Keep posts as in-memory `list[dict]` unless user asks for persistence.

## Python quality bar
- Add type annotations for new/updated functions.
- Add Google-style docstrings for new/updated functions.
- Keep functions small and readable; avoid unnecessary abstractions for this learning project.

## Template conventions
- Extend `templates/layout.html` for pages.
- Preserve Bootstrap structure and existing dark-mode behavior.
- Keep template logic minimal; prefer preparing data in route handlers.

## Safety and workflow
- Do not revert unrelated local changes.
- Make minimal, focused edits.
- After substantial edits, check lint diagnostics and fix introduced issues.
- check for ruff issues and fix those issues
